=== layout: one-panel
@replaceme


@body

![Slide image 8](assets/lect13c-chromo_alter_4-translocation/image_008.png)

- For the reciprocal translocation of two chromosomes.
- One product solution is...
- [\*\*ABCDE-TUV\*\*]{color=orange}  and [\*\*MNOPQRS-FG\*\*]{color=#1E6A39}
- Another product solution is...
- [\*\*ABCDE-SRQPONM\*\*]{color=red}  and [\*\*GF-TUV\*\*]{color=#355269}
- The telomeres are always attached to A, G, M, and V.

=== layout: one-panel
@replaceme


@body

![Slide image 8](assets/lect13c-chromo_alter_4-translocation/image_008.png)

- Reciprocal translocation of two chromosomes.
- 	\*\*ABCDE &#8211;  &#8211; FG\*\*
- \*\*MNOPQRS &#8211; &#8211; TUV\*\*
- TUV[\*\*]{color=red} &#8211; FG\*\*
- Cannot happen because the telomeres would be in the center of the chromosome.

=== layout: one-panel
@replaceme


@body

![Slide image 8](assets/lect13c-chromo_alter_4-translocation/image_008.png)

- Last question\: which product pairs are genetically stable?
- Pair 1\: [\*\*ABCDE-TUV\*\*]{color=orange}  and [\*\*MNOPQRS-FG\*\*]{color=#1E6A39}
- Pair 2\: [\*\*ABCDE-SRQPONM\*\*]{color=red}  and [\*\*GF-TUV\*\*]{color=#355269}
- [It depends on the location of the centromeres!]{color=red}
- [The problem does not tell us]{color=purple} the centromere locations&#8230; so let&#8217;s [pretend]{color=red} the centromeres are between C#D and P#Q

=== layout: one-panel


@body

![Slide image 8](assets/lect13c-chromo_alter_4-translocation/image_008.png)

- [The problem does not tell us]{color=purple} the centromere locations&#8230; so let&#8217;s [pretend]{color=red} the centromeres are between C#D and P#Q
- Pair 1\: [\*\*ABC]{color=orange}#[DE-TUV\*\*]{color=orange}  and [\*\*MNOP]{color=#1E6A39}#[QRS-FG\*\*]{color=#1E6A39}
- Pair 2\: [\*\*ABC]{color=red}#[DE-SRQ]{color=red}#[PONM\*\*]{color=red}  and [\*\*GF-TUV\*\*]{color=#355269}

=== layout: one-panel
@replaceme


@body

![Slide image 8](assets/lect13c-chromo_alter_4-translocation/image_008.png)

- [The problem does not tell us]{color=purple} the centromere locations&#8230; so let&#8217;s [pretend]{color=red} the centromeres are between C#D and P#Q
- Pair 1\: [\*\*ABC]{color=orange}#[DE-TUV\*\*]{color=orange}  and [\*\*MNOP]{color=#1E6A39}#[QRS-FG\*\*]{color=#1E6A39}
- Pair 2\: [\*\*ABC]{color=red}#[DE-SRQ]{color=red}#[PONM\*\*]{color=red}  and [\*\*GF-TUV\*\*]{color=#355269}
- Pair 1 has both monocentric chromosomes, this is good.
- Pair 2 has one dicentric and one acentric, this is genetically unstable

=== layout: one-panel


@body

![Slide image 8](assets/lect13c-chromo_alter_4-translocation/image_008.png)

- [Another one]{color=purple}&#8230; so let&#8217;s [pretend]{color=red} the centromeres are between C#D and T#U
- Pair 1\: [\*\*ABC]{color=orange}#[DE-T]{color=orange}#[UV\*\*]{color=orange}  and [\*\*MNOPQRS-FG\*\*]{color=#1E6A39}
- Pair 2\: [\*\*ABC]{color=red}#[DE-SRQPONM\*\*]{color=red}  and [\*\*GF-T]{color=#355269}#[UV\*\*]{color=#355269}
- Pair 1 has one dicentric and one acentric, this is genetically unstable
- Pair 2 has both monocentric chromosomes, this is good.
- It switched!

=== layout: one-panel


@body

![Slide image 8](assets/lect13c-chromo_alter_4-translocation/image_008.png)

- Summary
- (a) C-E inversion\: A B E D C F G
- (b) C-E deletion\: A B F G
- (c) A B C D E / T U V and M N O P Q R S / F G
- or A B C D E / S R Q P O M N and  V U T / F G
- (d) two monocentric -OR- dicentric and acentric pair
- (e) only monocentric chromosomes are stable

=== layout: one-panel

# *Typical Quiz Question*

@body

- Q1. Two chromosomes with the gene sequences ABCDEFGHJ and MPQRSTWXYZ undergo a reciprocal translocation after breaks between B|C and T|W.
- Which one of the following is [NOT]{color=red} a possible product of this translocation?
  - A. MPQRSTBA
  - B. MPQRSTCDEFGHJ
  - C. ZYXWCDEFGHJ
  - D. BAZYXW
  - E. ABWXYZ

=== layout: one-panel
@replaceme

# *Typical Quiz Question*

@body

- Q1. Two chromosomes with the gene sequences
- [\*AB&#8211;CDEFGHJ\*]{color=purple} and [\*MPQRST&#8211;WXYZ\*]{color=orange} undergo a reciprocal translocation after breaks between B|C and T|W.
- Which one of the following is [NOT]{color=red} a possible product of this translocation?
  - A. [\*MPQRST]{color=orange}&#8211;[BA\*]{color=purple}
  - B. [\*MPQRST]{color=orange}&#8211;[CDEFGHJ\*]{color=purple}
  - C. [\*ZYXW]{color=orange}&#8211;[CDEFGHJ\*]{color=purple}
  - D. [BA\*]{color=purple}&#8211;[\*ZYXW]{color=orange}
  - E. [\*AB]{color=purple}&#8211;[WXYZ\*]{color=orange}

- [Answer\: D]{color=red}

=== layout: one-panel

# *Typical Quiz Question*

@body

- Q2. Two chromosomes with the gene sequences ABCDEFGHJK and  QRSTWXY undergo a reciprocal translocation after breaks between G|H and W|X.
- Which one of the following is [NOT]{color=red} a possible product of this translocation?
  - A. YXGFEDCBA
  - B. ABCDEFGWTSRQ
  - C. YXHJK
  - D. KJHWTSRQ
  - E. HJKYX

=== layout: one-panel
@replaceme

# *Typical Quiz Question*

@body

- Q2. Two chromosomes with the gene sequences [\*ABCDEFG&#8211;HJK\*]{color=blue} and  [\*QRSTW&#8211;XY\*]{color=#B47804} undergo a reciprocal translocation after breaks between G|H and W|X.
- Which one of the following is [NOT]{color=red} a possible product of this translocation?
  - A. [\*YX]{color=#B47804}&#8211;[GFEDCBA\*]{color=blue}
  - B. [\*ABCDEFG]{color=blue}&#8211;[WTSRQ\*]{color=#B47804}
  - C. [\*YX]{color=#B47804}&#8211;[HJK\*]{color=blue}
  - D. [\*KJH]{color=blue}&#8211;[WTSRQ\*]{color=#B47804}
  - E. [HJK\*]{color=blue}&#8211;[\*YX]{color=#B47804}

- [Answer\: E]{color=red}

=== layout: bookend

# Key Takeaways

@body

- Translocations move DNA between chromosomes.
- Reciprocal translocations exchange chromosome segments.
- Unbalanced products have missing or extra DNA.
- Translocations can affect fertility and gene function.

